    "modelAnswer": "(i) $\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{x}{5}$, LCM $=60$: $=\\frac{30x+20x-15x+12x}{60}=\\frac{47x}{60}$\n\n(ii) $\\frac{1}{2}\\left(4-\\frac{x}{3}\\right)-\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}\\left(11-\\frac{x}{2}\\right)=2-\\frac{x}{6}-\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{11}{3}-\\frac{x}{6}=\\frac{29}{6}-\\frac{x}{3}=\\frac{29-2x}{6}$\n\n(iii) $\\frac{2}{x+1}+\\frac{x}{x-1}-\\frac{x+2}{x-1}=\\frac{2}{x+1}-\\frac{2}{x-1}=\\frac{2(x-1)-2(x+1)}{x^{2}-1}=\\frac{-4}{x^{2}-1}$\n\n(iv) $\\frac{x^{2}-25}{5}-\\frac{x}{4}\\div\\frac{3x}{20}$: since $\\frac{x}{4}\\div\\frac{3x}{20}=\\frac{x}{4}\\times\\frac{20}{3x}=\\frac{5}{3}$, this is $\\frac{x^{2}-25}{5}-\\frac{5}{3}=\\frac{3(x^{2}-25)-25}{15}=\\frac{3x^{2}-100}{15}$\n\n(v) $\\frac{45a^{2}b^{3}c^{4}}{27x^{4}y^{3}z}\\times\\frac{243xy^{2}z^{3}}{180a^{2}bc^{3}}=\\frac{9b^{2}cz^{2}}{4x^{3}y}$\n\n(vi) $\\frac{m^{2}}{8n}\\times\\frac{36p^{3}q^{2}}{81mn}\\div\\frac{15mpx^{5}}{270n^{2}x^{3}y}=\\frac{m^{2}}{8n}\\times\\frac{36p^{3}q^{2}}{81mn}\\times\\frac{270n^{2}x^{3}y}{15mpx^{5}}=\\frac{p^{2}q^{2}y}{x^{2}}$\n\n(vii) $3x\\div\\frac{3x^{2}-27}{x+3}+\\frac{1}{x-3}=3x\\times\\frac{x+3}{3(x-3)(x+3)}+\\frac{1}{x-3}=\\frac{x}{x-3}+\\frac{1}{x-3}=\\frac{x+1}{x-3}$\n\n(viii) $\\frac{5x+5}{3(2x-1)}+\\frac{6-2x}{2(1-2x)}=\\frac{5(x+1)}{3(2x-1)}+\\frac{x-3}{2x-1}=\\frac{10(x+1)+3(x-3)}{6(2x-1)}=\\frac{13x+1}{6(2x-1)}$\n\n(ix) $\\frac{2a}{2a-3}-\\frac{5}{6a+9}-\\frac{4(3a+2)}{3(4a^{2}-9)}$, common denom $3(4a^{2}-9)$: numerator $=6a(2a+3)-5(2a-3)-4(3a+2)=12a^{2}-4a+7$, so $=\\frac{12a^{2}-4a+7}{3(4a^{2}-9)}$\n\n(x) $\\frac{5}{5+x-18x^{2}}-\\frac{2}{2+5x+2x^{2}}$: $5+x-18x^{2}=(2x+1)(5-9x)$ and $2+5x+2x^{2}=(2x+1)(x+2)$, so $=\\frac{5(x+2)-2(5-9x)}{(2x+1)(5-9x)(x+2)}=\\frac{23x}{(2x+1)(5-9x)(x+2)}$\n\n(xi) $\\frac{m+3}{24m}-\\frac{m+1}{24m}+\\frac{3m-1}{6m^{2}+18m}\\div\\frac{12m-4}{m+3}$: first two terms give $\\frac{1}{12m}$; the division term gives $\\frac{3m-1}{6m(m+3)}\\times\\frac{m+3}{4(3m-1)}=\\frac{1}{24m}$; total $=\\frac{1}{12m}+\\frac{1}{24m}=\\frac{1}{8m}$\n\n(xii) $\\frac{1-p^{2}}{1+q}\\times\\frac{1-q^{2}}{p+p^{2}}\\times\\left(1+\\frac{p}{1-p}\\right)$: since $1+\\frac{p}{1-p}=\\frac{1}{1-p}$, and $1-p^{2}=(1-p)(1+p)$, $p+p^{2}=p(1+p)$, $1-q^{2}=(1-q)(1+q)$, everything cancels to $\\frac{1-q}{p}$\n\n(xiii) $\\left(1-\\frac{x}{1+\\frac{x}{1-x}}\\right)\\div(1+x^{3})$: since $1+\\frac{x}{1-x}=\\frac{1}{1-x}$, the inner term is $x(1-x)$, so the bracket is $1-x+x^{2}$; dividing by $1+x^{3}=(1+x)(1-x+x^{2})$ gives $\\frac{1}{1+x}$",
